---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Billing"
  description="How ACQI is licensed and invoiced: annual subscription per installation, invoiced in advance, no online checkout."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="micro micro--red mb-1 reveal">Commercial</p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal-2">Invoiced annually. No checkout button, on purpose.</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal reveal-3">
        An enterprise installation is not a card transaction. Licensing is quoted against a
        scope, signed on paper, and invoiced in advance. This page explains the mechanics so
        that finance and procurement can plan around them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">I</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">The model</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--2">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            A licence is granted per installation, for a defined estate, for twelve months. The
            fee covers the right to run the product in one environment, including its service
            tier, for any number of named operators up to the agreed limit.
          </p>
          <p>
            Price depends on the size of the estate and the module set you license. We do not
            publish a price list, because a per-seat figure without scope tells a buyer nothing
            and invites a comparison that does not hold.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-0">
            There is no consumption meter, no per-run charge and no charge for collector
            execution. A discovery cycle that reads four million objects costs the same as one
            that reads four thousand.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="micro mb-2">Included in a licence</p>
          <ul class="stack-list">
            <li>Product installation and updates for the licensed estate</li>
            <li>Shipped collectors and the migration workload set</li>
            <li>Support during business hours, named engineer</li>
            <li>Security releases at no additional cost</li>
            <li>Documentation and the export schema</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="micro mt-2 mb-1">Quoted separately</p>
          <p class="small mb-0">
            Deployment, estate read engagements, custom collectors, migration delivery support
            and training. See <a href="/services/">services</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">II</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Payment mechanics</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="defs">
        <div>
          <dt>Currency</dt>
          <dd>GBP or USD, fixed at the order. Invoices are not re-based mid-term.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Term</dt>
          <dd>Twelve months from the licence start date, invoiced annually in advance.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Method</dt>
          <dd>Bank transfer against an invoice. We do not take card payments, and there is no online checkout.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Payment terms</dt>
          <dd>Thirty days from invoice date, unless the order says otherwise.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Purchase orders</dt>
          <dd>Accepted. Put the PO number on the order and it will appear on the invoice.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Tax</dt>
          <dd>VAT is charged where applicable. Reverse-charge treatment applies for qualifying business customers in the EU. Once the entity is incorporated, the VAT number will appear on every invoice.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Late payment</dt>
          <dd>Statutory interest applies after the agreed terms. We will talk to you before we charge it.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Cancellation</dt>
          <dd>A licence can be ended at renewal with thirty days' notice. Mid-term termination is governed by the order and the <a href="/legal/terms/">terms</a>.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Refunds</dt>
          <dd>Fees are not refundable pro rata, except where the product does not perform as described and the fault is ours and cannot be corrected within a reasonable period.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">III</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Procurement</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Security review</h3>
          <p>A written questionnaire response is available under NDA. It includes items we cannot answer yet, marked as such rather than omitted.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Contracting entity</h3>
          <p>The entity is in formation. Orders placed now are made with the founders personally and will novate to the company on incorporation, on the same terms.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Invoicing details</h3>
          <p>Ask for the current invoice template and remittance details at the point of order. Bank details are never sent by email without a call-back verification.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="note mt-3">
        <p>
          <strong>On payment security.</strong> We will never email changed bank details. If you
          receive a message claiming to be us with new remittance information, call the number on
          your order before acting on it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-3 mb-0">
        <a class="btn btn--solid" href="/contact/">Request a quote</a>
        <span class="small" style="margin-left:1rem">Or email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.generalEmail}`}>{SITE.generalEmail}</a></span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
